{"7968":{"t":"From παύω (paúō, “stop, end”) + -σις (-sĭs).","d":[]},"7975":{"t":"From Proto-Indo-European *pelito-, from *pel- (“gray”). Cognates include Sanskrit प॒लि॒त (palitá), Latin pallidus and Old Armenian ալիք (alikʻ, “wave; gray hair”).","d":[]},"7959":{"t":"From παραλύω (paralúō) + -σις (-sis).","d":[]},"7980":{"t":"From πέντε (pénte, “five”) + -άκις (-ắkĭs, suffix for adverb of repetition).","d":[]},"7971":{"t":"From πεζός (pezós, “on foot”) + μάχη (mắkhē, “combat”) + -ία (-ĭ́ā).","d":[]},"7985":{"t":"Denominal verb from πέρα (péra, “beyond”); cognate with Albanian prura (“to bring, lead”).","d":["πέραμα","πιπράσκω"]},"7972":{"t":"Ellipsis of πεζῇ ὁδῷ (pezēî hodōî).","d":[]},"7936":{"t":"From παραπετάννυμαι (parapetánnumai, “to be hung before”) + -μα (-ma).","d":[]},"7907":{"t":"From παρα- (para-) + αἴτιος (aítios, “responsible, culpable”).","d":[]},"7967":{"t":"Ultimately from παύω (paúō, “to stop, abate”).","d":[]},"7958":{"t":"From παραλλάσσω (părăllắssō, “to cause to alternate”) + -σις (-sĭs).","d":[]},"7986":{"t":"From περι- (perĭ-, around) + δεῖπνον (deîpnon, “meal”).","d":[]},"7941":{"t":"From παρειά (păreiá, “cheek”) + -ας (-ās, nominal suffix), after the light spots on both sides of the neck.","d":[]},"7903":{"t":"From παρα- (para-) + πλόος (plóos) and/or παραπλέω (parapléō) + -ος (-os).","d":[]},"7906":{"t":"From παραινέω (parainéō) (from παρα- (para-) + αἰνέω (ainéō)) + -σις (-sis)","d":[]},"7950":{"t":"From παρήγορος (parḗgoros, “consoling, comforting”) (from παρα- (para-) + ἀγορεύω (agoreúō)) + -έω (-éō).","d":["paregoric","παρηγορικός"]}}